  "closed_execution_category": "Production FD/network compatibility RPC, including actual resource dependencies and refusal paths",
  "implementation": [
    "Original Send+Sync console byte resources bound once to actual OFDs; dup/fork/accepted I/O preserve resource identity after close/reuse. Same-thread UI/captured bytes; potentially blocking native descriptors use the existing bounded file pool. No new coordinator/resource/reader thread or polling bus; standalone CLI stdin reader removed.",
    "Complete original epoll control and legacy/nested watch graph retained through source creation, close, fork, SCM_RIGHTS and retirement; existing poll/control admission remains explicit.",
    "lseek/fstat retain original descriptions rather than incomplete query projections; no guest memory policy/fence added.",
    "Source byte EPIPE returns its final errno and signals the original task once. No failed byte operation replays on owner merely to deliver SIGPIPE. MSG_NOSIGNAL retains errno without signal.",
    "Removed Service event, Request/ReturnTo/reply transport and source wait, service_candidate, process_service owner handler, namespace stream-mask capture, Linux::network_service, run-queue/domain in-flight service state, and private legacy additive-mmap RPC. Local VM execution requires original task custody.",
    "Historical transport-only tests and the test-only cost experiment retire with their deleted transport. Original lifecycle, I/O/resource, seccomp, output-fault and close/reuse behaviors remain covered. Public old service counters remain zero-valued product diagnostics."
  ],
